From f3eae2ea7f99ae8a78dd84bcd3b611cbdb65d2a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:33:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 274/274] minicargo: build cdylib libraries; `--lib`,
 `--crate-type`, `--link-arg`, build-script link args

maturin builds a Python extension module with `cargo rustc --lib --crate-type cdylib`
(plus link args, see the previous trans patch); pyo3-build-config's
add_extension_module_link_args prints `cargo:rustc-cdylib-link-arg=-undefined` and
`=dynamic_lookup`. minicargo built a `cdylib` library as an rlib ("only ever consumed
as a Rust dependency"), had no `--lib`/`--crate-type`, and ignored every
`cargo:rustc-link-arg*` line.

- The root package's library gets a `--crate-type cdylib` compiler run beside the rlib
  when its crate types list `cdylib`, as 0148 does for `staticlib` (the two now share
  the FinalLib job kind); output lib<name>.dylib for -apple- targets, .dll for
  -windows, else .so, as cargo names it.
- `--crate-type <types>` (repeatable, comma-separated) replaces the manifest's crate
  types of the root library; `--lib` builds only the library. `--lib` with only
  non-Rust types (maturin) skips the rlib: one compilation of the crate, not two.
- `--link-arg <arg>` and the package's own build-script `rustc-link-arg`,
  `rustc-link-arg-cdylib` (= `rustc-cdylib-link-arg`), `rustc-link-arg-bins`,
  `rustc-link-arg-bin=BIN=`, `rustc-link-arg-tests` become `-C link-arg=` on the links
  they are meant for (cargo applies them only to the package that printed them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
